{"tool_name":"cython","contents":["neubias"],"fetched_metadata":{"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"basic_html","processed":"<p>The <a href=\"https://cython.org/\">Cython</a> language is a superset of the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://biii.eu/python\">Python</a>&nbsp;language that additionally supports calling&nbsp;<strong>C functions</strong>&nbsp;and declaring&nbsp;<strong>C types</strong>&nbsp;on variables and class attributes. This allows the compiler to generate very&nbsp;<strong>efficient C code</strong>&nbsp;from Cython code. This makes Cython the ideal language for&nbsp;<strong>wrapping</strong>&nbsp;external C libraries,&nbsp;<strong>embedding</strong>&nbsp;CPython into existing applications, and for&nbsp;<strong>fast C modules</strong>&nbsp;that speed up the execution of Python code.</p>","summary":"","value":"<p>The <a href=\"https://cython.org/\">Cython</a> language is a superset of the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://biii.eu/python\">Python</a>&nbsp;language that additionally supports calling&nbsp;<strong>C functions</strong>&nbsp;and declaring&nbsp;<strong>C types</strong>&nbsp;on variables and class attributes. This allows the compiler to generate very&nbsp;<strong>efficient C code</strong>&nbsp;from Cython code. This makes Cython the ideal language for&nbsp;<strong>wrapping</strong>&nbsp;external C libraries,&nbsp;<strong>embedding</strong>&nbsp;CPython into existing applications, and for&nbsp;<strong>fast C modules</strong>&nbsp;that speed up the execution of Python code.</p>\r\n"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2023-04-26T15:20:36+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2018-09-09T20:49:25+00:00"}],"default_langcode":[{"value":true}],"attribution_instructions":[],"comments_2023":[],"free_tagging":[],"give_feedback_on_this_soft":[{"cid":0,"comment_count":0,"last_comment_name":null,"last_comment_timestamp":1536526165,"last_comment_uid":161,"status":2}],"has_author":[],"has_biological_terms":[],"has_comparison":[],"has_documentation":[{"op